        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 25 at 3:15AM EDT until September 27 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Wind Advisory, northeast winds 25 to 35 mph with
gusts up to 45 mph. For the High Wind Warning, north winds 30 to 40
mph with gusts up to 60 mph expected.

* WHERE...In Delaware, Delaware Beaches County. In New Jersey,
Eastern Monmouth, Atlantic Coastal Cape May, Coastal Atlantic, and
Coastal Ocean Counties.

* WHEN...For the Wind Advisory, until 6 PM EDT this evening. For the
High Wind Warning, from 6 PM this evening to 6 AM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.
Power outages are possible. Travel will be difficult, especially
for high profile vehicles. Gusty winds will blow around unsecured
objects.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Strong winds may continue into Sunday,
depending on the track of the storm.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.

Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.

Secure outdoor objects.</instruction>
